        <div class="wrapper">
            <div id="topbg"></div>
            <h1 style="margin-top: 15px"><a href="http://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/" target="_blank"><img src="./S_T Phosphatases_files/LinearSignature_RGB.png" alt="National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute" style="border-style: none"></a></h1>
            <h1><a href="http://esbl.nhlbi.nih.gov/" target="_blank"><img src="./S_T Phosphatases_files/ESBL1.png" alt="Epithelial Systems Biology Laboratory (ESBL)" style="border-style: none"></a></h1>
            <br>
            <h1>Aldosterone Target Genes in Collecting Duct</h1>
         
            <div>
                
                <p>					
					This database is a compendium of mineralocortocoid receptor (Nr3c2) target genes from multiple publications.  References are given as PMID numbers. 
                </p>
				<p>
					Database was created by Angela Mak and Mark Knepper in the <a href="http://esbl.nhlbi.nih.gov/" target="_blank">Epithelial Systems Biology Laboratory</a> (Mark Knepper, Chief) at the <strong>National Heart, Lung and Blood Institute</strong> as part of its <a href="https://hpcwebapps.cit.nih.gov/ESBL/Database/" target="_blank">Kidney Systems Biology Project</a>. </p>
 					                 <p>
					
					<!--Click to <a href="https://esbl.nhlbi.nih.gov/Databases/KSBP2/Targets/Lists/Phosphatases/PhosphataseCatalyticSubunitWebsiteData.xlsx" target="_blank">download</a> processed data as spreadsheet. -->
				
				</p>
